  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nFollowing remnant convection off the Caprock early Sunday morning,\nthe remainder of the day is looking downright chilly and dreary \nas a cold front overspreads the region on damp NE winds. NBM remains\ntoo optimistic with highs in the 50s most everywhere, so these were\ntraded for 40s for the majority of the forecast area. Soundings \nshow sufficiently thick stratus for much of the day from I27 on east\nsupportive of drizzle, and this is reflected by the NBM's 20-40 PoPs\nthrough the day. Drizzle may continue on/off overnight into Monday\nmorning until the stratus depth shrinks to less than 1000 meters or\nso during the afternoon. Highs on Monday will also be curbed to \n15-20 degrees below normal in this \"stratus quo\" regime.\n\nTuesday still shows some hope for breaks in the stratus (especially\nnear the NM border) as moist upslope winds veer S-SW underneath \ndeeper drying from 850-700 mb. Fortunately, min temps are forecast\nto stay enough above freezing both Monday and Tuesday mornings \nthereby squashing freezing drizzle concerns.\n\nFollowing upper ridging earlier in the week, we return to an \nunsettled SW flow regime by late week supportive of low PoPs ahead\nof a potentially large and vigorous upper low entering the Great \nBasin. High temps will slowly improve into the 60s by mid/late \nweek.",
